<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);IDE0130</NoWarn>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <SatelliteResourceLanguages>en</SatelliteResourceLanguages>
    <Title>Simple Geometry Library</Title>
    <AssemblyVersion>2.0.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>2.0.0.0</FileVersion>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <Version>2.0.0.0</Version>
    <Description>A small, fast geometry library for games and real-time applications: points, vectors, rectangles, circles, ellipses, triangles, polygons, rays, planes, spheres, cubes, AABBs, capsules, and N-dimensional vectors.

Every shape is an immutable value type (readonly struct), so building one per frame or running thousands of intersection tests in a tight loop allocates nothing and adds no GC pressure. Shapes carry value equality (==, Equals, GetHashCode) and work correctly as dictionary keys. Includes intersection and containment tests, distances, area / volume / perimeter, and arithmetic operators.

Coordinates are stored as float — the library trades precision for speed and is not intended for CAD or scientific computing. Rectangle, Cube, and AABB are axis-aligned (no rotation).

MIT licensed.</Description> 
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Folder Include="Objects\2d\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
